                        "entry_id": "32ae5c87-a7f4-31aa-9eb4-b57a04e6f3d7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A bird of species of partridge native to central Asia (Alectoris chukar)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b95fb457-c293-470d-b364-f9e3d8fe1d9e",
                                "sense_id": "45d952eb-baed-326a-9276-abe4897d4a9a",
                                "text": "The black partridge is very noisy during the spring, which corresponds with its breeding season, and calls loud and incessantly in the morning, at midday, and sometimes even at night; the painted partridge has a pleasant chirping note; the chukar is another noisy bird; its call-note is fully described by Hume."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7d0cd401-7cd6-400e-ac29-d16ac3220aac",
                                "sense_id": "45d952eb-baed-326a-9276-abe4897d4a9a",
                                "text": "The climate is dry and at the time the chukars hatch that Is In their favor."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6a1082cd-8158-461a-9bec-8c200c0512b5",
                                "sense_id": "45d952eb-baed-326a-9276-abe4897d4a9a",
                                "text": "I bagged this one on Michigan's upper peninsula. ruffed grouse to be more difficult to hit, but the chukar is the most difficult to get to. I have hunted chukar when they held tight to the point of a dog and the .410 was plenty of gun, but I have also hunted them when the 12-gauge was none too much."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
